A||N||1||julzmiksch||Rack and pinion||||12||
Z||000000||julzmiksch||04-23-2001||06:16 PM||||Hi all! Quick female question...  how difficult is it to replace the rack and pinion in an '88 Formula?||||reg||12
Z||000001||DRH||04-23-2001||06:28 PM||||Not that bad. I would recommend taking the spare tire 'tub' out first. The few minutes it takes is well worth it for the extra working room.<P>- Remove 3(?) small screws inside the passenger compartment that attach a plastic sleeve that fits around the steering shaft so it can be slid up into the passenger compartment.<P>- Remove the pinch bolt that attaches the shaft to the rack.<P>- Remove outer tie rod; cotter pins and nuts and remove outer tie rod (I usually leave the nut just on and pop it with a hammer to get it loose).<P>- Four bolts hold the rack on. These are likely to be rusty and a little bit of a pain to break loose.<P>- Installation is reverse of removal  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>||||reg||1
